<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

    A launchd agent for running the monitor on a Mac that is left on.

    This is not the same thing as the «Автозапуск» checkbox in the settings:
    that writes an agent of its own, tied to the binary's current path, and is
    the right answer for a laptop somebody uses. This one is installed by hand
    and says where the log goes, which is what a machine nobody sits at needs.

        cp com.blanktrail.wbmon.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
        $EDITOR ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.blanktrail.wbmon.plist   # the path
        launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.blanktrail.wbmon.plist

    The password for the panel is printed on the first start and written to
    first-run.txt in the data directory:

        tail -n 20 /tmp/wbmon.log

    A LaunchAgent rather than a LaunchDaemon, and the same reasoning as
    everywhere else here: a monitor is one person's tool watching one person's
    listings. A daemon would run as root to solve a problem nobody has, and the
    database, the proxy key and the bot token all live under that person's home
    directory where their own permissions already protect them.

    RunAtLoad without KeepAlive, deliberately. A person who quits the monitor
    expects it to stay quit until the next login; KeepAlive would start it again
    a second later and look like a program that cannot be closed. Add KeepAlive
    only on a machine that is meant to be a server.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.blanktrail.wbmon</string>

	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<!-- The absolute path to the binary. No -open on a machine nobody is
		     sitting at: the panel is reached over an ssh tunnel, and opening a
		     browser at login is what the checkbox in the settings is for. -->
		<string>/Applications/wbmon/wbmon</string>
		<string>-open=false</string>
	</array>

	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>

	<!-- The data directory, if it should not be the default
	     (~/Library/Application Support/BlankTrail/wbmon).
	<key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
	<dict>
		<key>WBMON_DATA</key>
		<string>/Users/Shared/wbmon</string>
	</dict>
	-->

	<!-- Both streams into one file: the address and the password are printed on
	     the first start, and a person looking for them should not have to know
	     which stream they came out of.

	     /tmp rather than ~/Library/Logs, because launchd does not expand a
	     tilde and this file has to be copyable without knowing whose Mac it
	     lands on. Change it to an absolute path under the home directory if the
	     log should survive a restart. -->
	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/tmp/wbmon.log</string>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/tmp/wbmon.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
